---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="On building, thinking, and the space between engineering and wisdom.">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-20">
    <span class="section-label">// about</span>
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-display font-bold mt-4 mb-12 leading-tight" style="color: var(--v8-bone);">
      Building in uncertain domains
    </h1>

    <div class="prose max-w-none space-y-8">
      <p class="text-xl leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--v8-stone);">
        I'm Kevin Ong — an engineer based in San Francisco. I started in neural interface
        research, spent three years building electrode arrays in Ed Boyden's lab, and have
        been chasing variations of the same question ever since: how does a person actually
        get better at something?
      </p>

      <p class="leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--v8-stone);">
        That question has pulled me through ML for financial stress testing, automation at
        Palo Alto Networks, experimental hardware R&D at Desktop Metal, and now cloud
        infrastructure for educational gaming at IvyBee. The constant isn't the domain — it's
        the pattern: I end up in rooms where nothing exists yet and someone needs to design
        the first version.
      </p>

      <p class="leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--v8-stone);">
        On the side I'm building Meridian, an adaptive interview prep system that maps your
        knowledge state across a skill graph and generates targeted practice. It grew out of
        EarWorm, an earlier project where I used a hierarchical VQ-VAE to decompose the skill
        space of piano performance. Different domains, same architecture of thinking.
      </p>

      <div class="pl-6 py-4 my-12" style="border-left: 3px solid var(--v8-warm);">
        <p class="italic text-lg leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--v8-stone);">
          I'm wide, not deep — but I learn fast, and I deliver. The most useful thing
          about me is the architecture instinct that comes from building across enough
          different domains to see the patterns that transfer.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--v8-stone);">
        This site is where I write about what I'm learning. Essays on adaptive systems sit
        alongside reflections on meditation practice. Technical dives coexist with thoughts
        on Sibelius and winter listening. The connections between these domains are where
        the interesting insights tend to emerge.
      </p>

      <p class="leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--v8-stone);">
        When I'm not building or writing, you'll find me deep in a classical music rabbit hole
        (Rachmaninoff, Sibelius, and Mahler), practicing meditation badly,
        or being supervised by Princess, a ragdoll who has strong opinions about my code.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-16 pt-8" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--v8-deep);">
        <span class="section-label">// this_site</span>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed mt-4" style="color: var(--v8-stone);">
          Built with Astro, designed for reading, optimized for ideas worth your attention.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
